      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://ubuntu.com/security/notices/USN-6678-1",
        "name": "USN-6678-1",
        "description": "It was discovered that libgit2 mishandled equivalent filenames on NTFS partitions. If a user or automated system were tricked into cloning a specially crafted repository, an attacker could possibly use this issue to execute arbitrary code. This issue only affected Ubuntu 16.04 LTS and Ubuntu 18.04 LTS. (CVE-2020-12278, CVE-2020-12279)  It was discovered that libgit2 did not perform certificate checking by default. An attacker could possibly use this issue to perform a machine-in-the-middle attack. This issue only affected Ubuntu 16.04 LTS, Ubuntu 18.04 LTS, Ubuntu 20.04 LTS, and Ubuntu 22.04 LTS. (CVE-2023-22742)  It was discovered that libgit2 could be made to run into an infinite loop. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of service. This issue only affected Ubuntu 23.10. (CVE-2024-24575)  It was discovered that libgit2 did not properly manage memory. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of service or execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2024-24577)",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2024-24575"
        ]
      },
      "timestamp": "2024-03-05T18:46:35Z",
